{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1056827","formula":"H₂Zn","hill":"H2Zn","elements":["H","Zn"],"composition":{"H":2.0,"Zn":1.0},"names":{"en":"Zinc hydride","ru":"Гидрид цинка"},"descriptions":{"en":"Zinc hydride is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula ZnH2. It is a white, odourless solid which slowly decomposes into its elements at room temperature; despite this it is the most stable of the binary first row transition metal hydrides. A variety of coordination compounds containing Zn–H bonds are used as reducing agents, but ZnH2 itself has no common applications.","ru":"Гидри́д ци́нка — бинарное неорганическое соединение цинка и водорода с формулой ZnH 2 {\\displaystyle {\\ce {ZnH2}}} . Является белым кристаллическим веществом без запаха, которое медленно разлагается при комнатной температуре. Несмотря на это, гидрид цинка является самым стабильным из бинарных гидридов переходных металлов первого ряда."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":22056524,"mass":67.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"[H-].[H-].[Zn+2]","inchikey":"BSDVKYDHDPXIIG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"zinc hydride","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"22056524","atoms":3,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.493,"y":-0.039,"z":-0.182,"el":"H"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":2.493,"y":0.039,"z":0.182,"el":"Zn"}],"bonds":[]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1056827","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zinc_hydride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D0%B8%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B4_%D1%86%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://